<para><anchor id="Specification_tree_ref_1md_pdi_2docs_2Specification__tree__ref"/></para>
<para>The PDI specification tree is expressed in <ref refid="YAML" kindref="compound">YAML</ref>. This reference documents each key of the tree in its own section, named by the full path that leads to it from the root of the tree.</para>
<para>The paths follow these conventions:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>a dot <computeroutput>.</computeroutput> separates a key from the key that contains it, <emphasis>e.g.</emphasis> <computeroutput>logging.output.file</computeroutput> is the <computeroutput>file</computeroutput> key of the <computeroutput>output</computeroutput> mapping of the <computeroutput>logging</computeroutput> mapping at the root of the tree,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>a name between angle brackets is a key whose name you choose, <emphasis>e.g.</emphasis> <computeroutput>data.&lt;data_name&gt;</computeroutput> is any key of the <computeroutput>data</computeroutput> mapping,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>[*]</computeroutput> stands for any element of a sequence, <emphasis>e.g.</emphasis> <computeroutput>include[*]</computeroutput>,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>where a key accepts either a single value or a sequence of such values, the paths below it are written for the single value, and they apply to each element of the sequence alike.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Datatypes and $-expressions can be found at many places in the tree, including in the configuration of plugins. Each is documented once, in its own page: <ref refid="Spectree_types_ref" kindref="compound">Datatypes</ref> and <ref refid="spectree_expression" kindref="compound">$-expressions</ref>. The paths of the keys of a datatype start from the datatype itself, <emphasis>e.g.</emphasis> <computeroutput>&lt;array&gt;.size</computeroutput> is the <computeroutput>size</computeroutput> key of a datatype whose <computeroutput>type</computeroutput> is <computeroutput>array</computeroutput>, wherever that datatype appears.</para>
<para>The root of the specification tree is a mapping. Keys not listed in this reference are ignored at the root of the tree.</para>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_example">
<title>Example of a specification tree</title><para><programlisting filename=".yaml"><codeline><highlight class="normal">include:<sp/>my_other_configuration_file.yml</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">logging:<sp/>trace</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">types:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>metadata_t:<sp/>int</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">metadata:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>my_metadata:<sp/>metadata_t</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">data:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>my_data:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>type:<sp/>array</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>subtype:<sp/>double</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>size:<sp/>$my_metadata</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">plugin_path:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>-<sp/>/usr/lib/pdi</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">plugins:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>decl_hdf5:<sp/>#...</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>mpi:<sp/>#...</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_include">
<title><computeroutput>include</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Optional.</emphasis> Other YAML files, or subtrees of files, that hold parts of the same specification tree.</para>
<para>The value is either a single include directive or a sequence of include directives. An include directive is either:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>a scalar, the path of a file whose root is included, a shortcut for a mapping whose <computeroutput>file</computeroutput> is that scalar and whose <computeroutput>subtree</computeroutput> is empty,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>a mapping with both an <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_include_file" kindref="member"><computeroutput>include.file</computeroutput></ref> and an <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_include_subtree" kindref="member"><computeroutput>include.subtree</computeroutput></ref> key, and no other key.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>An included tree has the same format as the root of the specification tree. Its <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_include" kindref="member"><computeroutput>include</computeroutput></ref>, <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_types" kindref="member"><computeroutput>types</computeroutput></ref>, <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_metadata" kindref="member"><computeroutput>metadata</computeroutput></ref>, <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_data" kindref="member"><computeroutput>data</computeroutput></ref>, <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_plugin_path" kindref="member"><computeroutput>plugin_path</computeroutput></ref> and <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_plugins" kindref="member"><computeroutput>plugins</computeroutput></ref> keys are taken into account, while its <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_logging" kindref="member"><computeroutput>logging</computeroutput></ref> key is ignored. The keys under these sections must not be repeated: a type, a data, a metadata or a plugin defined in two files is an error.</para>
<para>The same file can be included twice (diamond include) but recursive inclusion is an error.</para>
<sect2 id="Specification_tree_ref_1example-of-include">
<title>Example of <computeroutput>include</computeroutput></title><para><programlisting filename=".yaml"><codeline><highlight class="normal">include:<sp/>my_other_configuration_file.yml</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>is interpreted as if it was:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".yaml"><codeline><highlight class="normal">include:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>-<sp/>file:<sp/>my_other_configuration_file.yml</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>subtree:<sp/>&quot;&quot;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_include_file">
<title><computeroutput>include.file</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Required in a mapping include directive.</emphasis> A scalar, the path of the file to include. The path is interpreted relative to the working directory of the execution.</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_include_subtree">
<title><computeroutput>include.subtree</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Required in a mapping include directive.</emphasis> A scalar, the ypath of the subtree to include from <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_include_file" kindref="member"><computeroutput>include.file</computeroutput></ref>, empty for the root of the file.</para>
<para>The subtree ypath is expanded according to the ypath specification of paraconf:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>access to a mapping element using the dot syntax: <emphasis>e.g.</emphasis> <computeroutput>.map.key</computeroutput></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>access to a sequence element using square brackets (indices are 0-based): <emphasis>e.g.</emphasis> <computeroutput>.seq[1]</computeroutput></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>access to a mapping element key using braces (indices are 0-based): <emphasis>e.g.</emphasis> <computeroutput>.map{1}</computeroutput></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>access to a mapping element value by index using chevrons: <emphasis>e.g.</emphasis> <computeroutput>.map&lt;1&gt;</computeroutput></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<sect2 id="Specification_tree_ref_1example-of-includesubtree">
<title>Example of <computeroutput>include.subtree</computeroutput></title><para><programlisting filename=".yaml"><codeline><highlight class="normal">include:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>-<sp/>file:<sp/>&quot;/my/file.yaml&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>subtree:<sp/>&quot;.pdi&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>-<sp/>file:<sp/>&quot;relative_file.yaml&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>subtree:<sp/>&quot;[1]&quot;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_logging">
<title><computeroutput>logging</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Optional.</emphasis> The configuration of the logger of PDI. It is only read from the root file, not from included ones. Each plugin has its own logger, configured by the <computeroutput>logging</computeroutput> key of its own configuration, with the same keys as below (see <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_plugins_plugin_name_logging" kindref="member"><computeroutput>plugins.&lt;plugin_name&gt;.logging</computeroutput></ref>).</para>
<para>The value is either:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>a scalar, a shortcut for a mapping whose only key is <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_logging_level" kindref="member"><computeroutput>logging.level</computeroutput></ref> with that value,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>a mapping with the keys below.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<sect2 id="Specification_tree_ref_1example-of-logging">
<title>Example of <computeroutput>logging</computeroutput></title><para><programlisting filename=".yaml"><codeline><highlight class="normal">logging:<sp/>&quot;debug&quot;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_logging_level">
<title><computeroutput>logging.level</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Optional.</emphasis> A scalar, the verbosity level of the logger. It can be set to (from the most to the least verbose):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>&quot;trace&quot;</computeroutput> - shows a log for every step of the execution, to debug the library itself,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>&quot;debug&quot;</computeroutput> - shows a log when a normal situation of the execution might be useful to understand the behavior of the library,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>&quot;info&quot;</computeroutput> - shows a log when a normal situation of the execution is likely useful to understand the behavior of the library,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>&quot;warn&quot;</computeroutput> - shows a log when a very likely invalid situation has been detected by the library (user input that is technically valid, but very unusual for example),</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>&quot;error&quot;</computeroutput> - shows a log when an invalid situation has been detected by the library (invalid user input, invalid hardware behaviour, etc.),</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>&quot;off&quot;</computeroutput> - logs are disabled.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>By default, the level is <computeroutput>info</computeroutput> for PDI and the level of PDI for a plugin.</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_logging_pattern">
<title><computeroutput>logging.pattern</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Optional.</emphasis> A scalar, the spdlog pattern of a log line.</para>
<para>The pattern is parsed by the spdlog library (see <ulink url="https://github.com/gabime/spdlog/wiki/3.-Custom-formatting">https://github.com/gabime/spdlog/wiki/3.-Custom-formatting</ulink>). It specifies the format of the whole line, so it should contain <computeroutput>v</computeroutput>, the logged message itself.</para>
<para>PDI introduces a new special flag, <computeroutput>%{&lt;REF&gt;}</computeroutput>, where <computeroutput>&lt;REF&gt;</computeroutput> is the <computeroutput>REFERENCE</computeroutput> part of a <ref refid="spectree_expression" kindref="compound">$-expressions</ref> without its leading <computeroutput>$</computeroutput> (with an optional format specification). It is evaluated just after all plugins have been initialized.</para>
<para>By default, the pattern is (where <computeroutput>n</computeroutput> is <computeroutput>PDI</computeroutput> or a plugin name): <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">[%T][%n]<sp/>***<sp/>%^%l%$:<sp/>%v</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> for serial execution and: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">[%T][MPI<sp/>%{MPI_COMM_WORLD_rank:06d}][%n]<sp/>***<sp/>%^%l%$:<sp/>%v</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> when the <ref refid="mpi_plugin" kindref="compound">MPI plugin</ref> is loaded. The pattern of a plugin defaults to that of PDI.</para>
<sect2 id="Specification_tree_ref_1example-of-loggingpattern">
<title>Example of <computeroutput>logging.pattern</computeroutput></title><para><programlisting filename=".yaml"><codeline><highlight class="normal">logging:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>level:<sp/>&quot;debug&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>pattern:<sp/>&quot;[%{MPI_COMM_WORLD_rank:04d}][%n][%l]<sp/>%v&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">plugins:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>mpi:</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_logging_output">
<title><computeroutput>logging.output</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Optional.</emphasis> A mapping, the destinations of the logs, with the keys below.</para>
<sect2 id="Specification_tree_ref_1example-of-loggingoutput">
<title>Example of <computeroutput>logging.output</computeroutput></title><para><programlisting filename=".yaml"><codeline><highlight class="normal">logging:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>level:<sp/>&quot;debug&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>output:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>file:<sp/>&quot;test.log&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>console:<sp/>&quot;on&quot;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_logging_output_file">
<title><computeroutput>logging.output.file</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Optional.</emphasis> A scalar, the path of a file where to write the logs.</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_logging_output_console">
<title><computeroutput>logging.output.console</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Optional.</emphasis> A scalar, <computeroutput>on</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>off</computeroutput>, whether to write the logs on the standard output. Only the exact value <computeroutput>off</computeroutput> disables the console, any other value enables it.</para>
<para>By default, it is <computeroutput>off</computeroutput> when <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_logging_output_file" kindref="member"><computeroutput>logging.output.file</computeroutput></ref> is defined and <computeroutput>on</computeroutput> otherwise.</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_types">
<title><computeroutput>types</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Optional.</emphasis> A mapping, the user-defined datatypes.</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_types_type_name">
<title><computeroutput>types.&lt;type_name&gt;</computeroutput></title><para>A <ref refid="Spectree_types_ref_1spectree_datatype" kindref="member"><computeroutput>&lt;datatype&gt;</computeroutput></ref>, the definition of the datatype named <computeroutput>&lt;type_name&gt;</computeroutput>. <computeroutput>&lt;type_name&gt;</computeroutput> can then be used as the value of <ref refid="Spectree_types_ref_1spectree_datatype_type" kindref="member"><computeroutput>&lt;datatype&gt;.type</computeroutput></ref> anywhere a datatype is expected.</para>
<para>A user-defined datatype cannot reuse the name of an existing datatype.</para>
<sect2 id="Specification_tree_ref_1example-of-typestype_name">
<title>Example of <computeroutput>types.&lt;type_name&gt;</computeroutput></title><para><programlisting filename=".yaml"><codeline><highlight class="normal">types:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>vector3_t:<sp/>{type:<sp/>array,<sp/>subtype:<sp/>double,<sp/>size:<sp/>3}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">data:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>position:<sp/>vector3_t</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_metadata">
<title><computeroutput>metadata</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Optional.</emphasis> A mapping, the metadata exposed by the application. PDI keeps a copy of the value of a metadata when it is shared, so that it can be referenced in $-expressions afterwards.</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_metadata_data_name">
<title><computeroutput>metadata.&lt;data_name&gt;</computeroutput></title><para>A <ref refid="Spectree_types_ref_1spectree_datatype" kindref="member"><computeroutput>&lt;datatype&gt;</computeroutput></ref>, the type of the metadata named <computeroutput>&lt;data_name&gt;</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>A name can only be defined once among all <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_metadata" kindref="member"><computeroutput>metadata</computeroutput></ref> and <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_data" kindref="member"><computeroutput>data</computeroutput></ref> keys.</para>
<sect2 id="Specification_tree_ref_1example-of-metadatadata_name">
<title>Example of <computeroutput>metadata.&lt;data_name&gt;</computeroutput></title><para><programlisting filename=".yaml"><codeline><highlight class="normal">metadata:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>my_metadata_1:<sp/>int</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>my_metadata_2:<sp/>{type:<sp/>array,<sp/>subtype:<sp/>double,<sp/>size:<sp/>5}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_data">
<title><computeroutput>data</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Optional.</emphasis> A mapping, the data exposed by the application. Unlike for <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_metadata" kindref="member"><computeroutput>metadata</computeroutput></ref>, PDI only keeps a reference to a data while it is shared.</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_data_data_name">
<title><computeroutput>data.&lt;data_name&gt;</computeroutput></title><para>A <ref refid="Spectree_types_ref_1spectree_datatype" kindref="member"><computeroutput>&lt;datatype&gt;</computeroutput></ref>, the type of the data named <computeroutput>&lt;data_name&gt;</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>A name can only be defined once among all <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_metadata" kindref="member"><computeroutput>metadata</computeroutput></ref> and <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_data" kindref="member"><computeroutput>data</computeroutput></ref> keys.</para>
<sect2 id="Specification_tree_ref_1example-of-datadata_name">
<title>Example of <computeroutput>data.&lt;data_name&gt;</computeroutput></title><para><programlisting filename=".yaml"><codeline><highlight class="normal">data:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>my_data_1:<sp/>int</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>my_data_2:<sp/>{type:<sp/>array,<sp/>subtype:<sp/>double,<sp/>size:<sp/>5}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_plugin_path">
<title><computeroutput>plugin_path</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Optional.</emphasis> A scalar or a sequence of scalars, the path to directories where PDI should search for plugins.</para>
<para>PDI takes the first match, searching the directories of the <computeroutput>PDI_PLUGIN_PATH</computeroutput> environment variable first, then those of <computeroutput>plugin_path</computeroutput>, then the directory where PDI installs its plugins, and finally the system library path.</para>
<sect2 id="Specification_tree_ref_1example-of-plugin_path">
<title>Example of <computeroutput>plugin_path</computeroutput></title><para><programlisting filename=".yaml"><codeline><highlight class="normal">plugin_path:<sp/>&quot;/home/user123/plugins&quot;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><programlisting filename=".yaml"><codeline><highlight class="normal">plugin_path:<sp/>[&quot;/home/user123/plugins&quot;,<sp/>&quot;/usr/lib/pdi/plugins&quot;]</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_plugins">
<title><computeroutput>plugins</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Optional.</emphasis> A mapping, the plugins to load.</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_plugins_plugin_name">
<title><computeroutput>plugins.&lt;plugin_name&gt;</computeroutput></title><para>The configuration of the plugin named <computeroutput>&lt;plugin_name&gt;</computeroutput>, which PDI loads. Its content depends on the plugin: have a look at the <ref refid="Plugins" kindref="compound">plugins</ref> documentation to see the specification tree each accepts. It can be empty (<computeroutput>~</computeroutput>) for a plugin that needs no configuration.</para>
<para>A plugin can only be loaded once, even across included files.</para>
<sect2 id="Specification_tree_ref_1example-of-pluginsplugin_name">
<title>Example of <computeroutput>plugins.&lt;plugin_name&gt;</computeroutput></title><para><programlisting filename=".yaml"><codeline><highlight class="normal">plugins:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>trace:<sp/>~</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>decl_hdf5:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>file:<sp/>example.h5</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>write:<sp/>[my_data]</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_plugins_plugin_name_logging">
<title><computeroutput>plugins.&lt;plugin_name&gt;.logging</computeroutput></title><para><emphasis>Optional.</emphasis> The configuration of the logger of the plugin, with the same format as <ref refid="Specification_tree_ref_1spectree_logging" kindref="member"><computeroutput>logging</computeroutput></ref>. This key is handled by PDI for every plugin whose configuration is a mapping.</para>
<sect2 id="Specification_tree_ref_1example-of-pluginsplugin_namelogging">
<title>Example of <computeroutput>plugins.&lt;plugin_name&gt;.logging</computeroutput></title><para><programlisting filename=".yaml"><codeline><highlight class="normal">plugins:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>decl_hdf5:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>logging:<sp/>debug</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>file:<sp/>example.h5</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
